      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I understand you've confirmed it, but sertraline 1000 mg daily is far above any dose with a clinical indication. The maximum labeled dose is 200 mg/day, and I know of no protocol or condition that calls for 1000 mg. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, arrhythmia, and other serious harm. I can't enter it as a routine order.\n\nIf you think this dose is needed, these steps would work:\n- **Call pharmacy or psychiatry** to review it. They can verify the dose and document the rationale.\n- **Use your institution's override process.** This usually means a documented exception and a second clinician's sign-off. It shouldn't go through me as a standard entry.\n- **Enter a different dose now.** I can enter up to 200 mg by mouth once daily, or any lower dose, if that's useful.\n\nIf the 1000 mg was a typo or a unit mix-up, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it."
      }
